description: Enforce lite/full verify gates after Rust edits; never relax thresholds
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Gate contract

- After non-trivial Rust edits, run `./scripts/verify.sh lite` (or `/verify`
  lite) before claiming the change works.
- After dry-rs dogfood fixes, module splits, CRAP/coverage work, or finishing
  an “implement the plan” task, run `./scripts/verify.sh full` (or `/verify`).
- Never edit `clippy.toml`, CRAP `--threshold`, or `dry.toml` solely to hide
  failures or self-scan findings.
- Prefer [`scripts/verify.sh`](../../../scripts/verify.sh) over pasted ad-hoc
  command lists. See [`.agents/skills/verify-gates/SKILL.md`](../../skills/verify-gates/SKILL.md).
